    {
      "text": "Figure 2, ‘Overview of labour market components supported by the NHWA modules’. Three vertical columns connected by rightward arrows from left to right represent the three health labour market components and the 10 NHWA modules supporting them: (1) ‘Education’ (left, orange), containing ‘Module 2: Education and training’, ‘Module 3: Education and training regulation and accreditation’, and ‘Module 4: Education finances’; (2) ‘Labour Force’ (centre, pink), containing ‘Module 1: Active health workforce stock’, ‘Module 5: Health labour market flows’, ‘Module 6: Employment characteristics and working conditions’, and ‘Module 7: Health workforce spending and remuneration’; and (3) ‘Serving Population Health Needs’ (right, light blue), containing ‘Module 8: Skill-mix composition for models of care’, ‘Module 9: Governance and health workforce policies’, and ‘Module 10: Health workforce information systems’.",
